{
 "id": "l30",
 "label": "30",
 "title": "Verb roots",
 "summary": "The root is the basic form of a verb: add affixes to make verbs and adjectives, or put ang before it to make a noun",
 "minutes": 30,
 "goals": [
  "Understand what a verb root is",
  "See how affixes turn a root into tenses or adjectives",
  "Learn twelve roots and the verbs made from them",
  "Use ang (or ang mga) + root as the subject of a sentence"
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "What is a verb root?",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "A **verb root** is the **basic form** of a verb, such as **áral** (*study*)."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "When an **affix** (a prefix or other added part) is attached, the root takes on different **tenses**, or it can become an **adjective**:"
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Form",
      "What it is"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "[[nag-aral|pred]]",
       "the root in the **past tense**"
      ],
      [
       "[[mag-aarál|pred]]",
       "the root in the **future tense**"
      ],
      [
       "[[arál na tao|other]]",
       "the root as an **adjective**: educated person"
      ],
      [
       "[[kilaláng guró|other]]",
       "the root as an **adjective**: well-known teacher"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "One root, many forms",
     "note": "Lesson 14 showed this future as mag-aáral. The book writes guró here and gurò elsewhere."
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "remember",
     "title": "You have seen this before",
     "t": "In Lesson 14 you built -um- and mag- verbs from roots such as **alís** and **áral**: umalís, mag-áral. This lesson collects more roots and shows another use for them."
    }
   ]
  },
