     "title": "Verb roots"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "Two kinds of to know",
     "items": [
      "**málaman** (root **alám**): to know **things**.",
      "**mákilala** (root **kilála**): to know **persons**."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "Look closely",
     "items": [
      "Some roots change a little when the affix is added: dalá → **dalhín**, tanóng → **tanungín**, sagót → **sagutín**.",
      "The same root can make more than one verb: ayaw → **umayáw** (to decline or dislike) and **ayawán** (to be declined or disliked)."
     ]
